and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"209":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"210":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"213":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"214":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"215":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"216":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"217":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"218":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"219":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"220":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"221":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"222":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"223":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"224":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"225":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"226":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"227":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA storage before increasing VA replicas"},"228":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-40","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"managed OIDC roles and removal of evaluation credentials"},"229":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-41","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a trusted TLS issuer or externally managed certificate"},"230":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-42","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"resource requests, replicas, autoscaling, disruption budgets and placement"},"231":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-43","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"SMTP, observability and alert delivery"},"232":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-44","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"the migration notes in `charts/lamassu/CHANGELOG/` before every upgrade"},"233":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm-45","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"The complete values reference is maintained in `charts/lamassu/VALUES.md` in the Helm repository."},"234":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"page","content":"Expose the Gateway","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking"},"235":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-0","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","content":"Choose how clients reach Lamassu, when to set gateway.addresses and how to design multiple Gateways."},"236":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-1","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"Expose the Lamassu Gateway"},"237":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Do you need `gateway.addresses`?"},"238":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"Recommended single-node design"},"239":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s"},"240":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Bare metal with MetalLB or kube-vip"},"241":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"External reverse proxy, NAT or VPN"},"242":{"id":"/docs/deployment/self-ho