ister-device#if-the-result-fails","content":"If assignment fails, review permissions and operation diagnostics before repeating it. Query the device and its history again to find the persisted result."},"1491":{"id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device-48","page_id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device#if-the-result-fails","content":"If an expiration or renewal state appears, check certificate dates and DMS thresholds in Devices and identities."},"1492":{"id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device-49","page_id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device#automate-the-next-device","content":"Continue with DMS and EST for the device to request and renew certificates. Prepare server trust, the initial credential and policies for each operation before implementing the client."},"1493":{"id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device-50","page_id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device#automate-the-next-device","content":"For a path from the client through mTLS, follow Enroll and connect your first device with a new ID."},"1494":{"id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device-51","page_id":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/register-device#automate-the-next-device","content":"To use the identity in AWS IoT Core, also prepare trust and permissions in the destination. Check the connection from the device after installing the required key, certificate and chain."},"1495":{"id":"/docs/platform/overview","page_id":"/docs/platform/overview","type":"page","content":"Lamassu IoT Platform","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"ur